  "description": "Dashboards as code for .NET: derive Grafana dashboards and Prometheus alert rules from the System.Diagnostics.Metrics instruments your app already defines. MeterScan captures instrument name, kind, unit and description from live Meter objects via MeterListener; DashboardDeriver turns them into a RED-style Grafana dashboard (rate/errors/duration rows, histogram_quantile p50/p95/p99, unit-aware formatting, OpenTelemetry Prometheus exporter naming with _total suffixes) as deterministic, diff-friendly JSON pinned to a fixed schemaVersion; Slo generates multiwindow multi-burn-rate alerting and recording rules (the Google SRE workbook table) as Prometheus rule-file YAML with every PromQL expression in a literal block scalar. A thin fluent builder (timeseries, stat, gauge, table panels on an auto-computed grid, portable ${datasource} variable) is the plumbing underneath. Zero external dependencies.",
